{"timestamp":"2026-05-13T19:10:15.249Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Short answer: **Codex plugins do not get their own `/plugin-name` slash commands**. In Codex CLI, slash commands are built-ins like `/review` and `/plugins`. Installed plugins are invoked with `@plugin` or bundled skills with `$skill`.\n\nUse slash commands like this:\n\n```text\n/review        # built-in Codex review\n/plugins       # browse/install/toggle plugins\n/skills        # if your Codex build exposes it, choose installed skills\n```\n\nReview-related plugins worth using:\n\n| Plugin | Best for | Install |\n|---|---|---|\n| [GitHub](https://www.codex-marketplace.com/plugins/github) | PR review, review comments, CI failures | `npx codex-marketplace add openai/plugins/plugins/github --plugin --global` |\n| [Codex Reviewer](https://www.codex-marketplace.com/plugins/codex-reviewer) | stricter second-pass review | `npx codex-marketplace add schuettc/codex-reviewer --plugin --global` |\n| [HOTL](https://www.codex-marketplace.com/plugins/hotl) | plan, execute, review, verify workflow | `npx codex-marketplace add yimwoo/hotl-plugin --plugin --global` |\n| [Brooks Lint](https://www.codex-marketplace.com/plugins/brooks-lint) | architecture, tech debt, test-quality review | `npx codex-marketplace add hyhmrright/brooks-lint --plugin --global` |\n| [ATeam](https://www.codex-marketplace.com/plugins/ateam) | specialist `@Reviewer` role | `npx codex-marketplace add yimwoo/codex-agenteam --plugin --global` |\n| [Build Web Apps](https://www.codex-marketplace.com/plugins/build-web-apps) | web/UI review, React/Next guidance | `npx codex-marketplace add openai/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps --plugin --global` |\n\nAfter install/restart, invoke with examples like:\n\n```text\n@codex-reviewer review my current diff\n@github review this PR\n@Reviewer review the implementation\n$review-swarm review my current diff\n```\n\nSource note: OpenAI’s Codex docs say `/plugins` is the slash command for plugin browsing, while plugins/skills are explicitly invoked with `@` or `$`, not custom slash commands. See [Codex slash commands](https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/slash-commands) and [Codex plugins](https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins).","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
